# The BMAD tool installation itself is NOT tracked — removed 28 Aug 2026.
#
# `.claude/skills/` is 49 third-party skill packages and `_bmad/` is the
# framework install: 265 files and about 3 MB of somebody else's code, shipping
# with no licence text of its own. This repository's central claim is that
# every component's licence is enumerated and checked, and `npm run licence-audit`
# covers npm, Python, the models and vendored binaries — it never looked at
# either of these trees. Publishing un-audited third-party code beside that
# claim is the one inconsistency this project cannot afford, and the tooling is
# reinstallable in a command, so it goes.
#
# Install BMAD separately if you want to run its workflows; nothing the
# workbench does at runtime depends on it.
#
# `_bmad/custom/` IS kept: those overrides are ours, they explain themselves,
# and the build loop that produced them referred to them.
.claude/skills/
_bmad/*
!_bmad/custom/

# The development method's own working output, removed from the repository on
# 31 August 2026 and kept on disk.
#
# It was tracked in full for three days, on the reasoning that the specs say why
# each story was built the way it was and someone picking the project up cold
# would need them. That reasoning was sound for a teammate and wrong for a
# reader: what survives here should be the product and the evidence behind its
# decisions — the ADRs, the licence record, the measurements — not the process
# that produced them. The decisions are in docs/adr/; the measurements are in
# docs/measurements/; the history is in git.
_bmad/
_bmad-output/

# Claude Code worktrees — Lane B works in one; never commit a worktree tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# Story 5.4's approval-note tool writes real .docx files here at runtime
# (session cwd defaults to the repo root under `dsh --profile headless`).
# Generated output, never source.
/deliverables/

# Kept on disk, deliberately out of the repository (31 August 2026). CLAUDE.md is
# instruction for an AI coding agent, not part of the product; a reader of this
# repository should meet the README, not a briefing written for a tool.
CLAUDE.md

# `npm run record-demo` writes its MP4 here. Recordings are output, not source.
videos/
